  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186087879,
      "id": "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d",
      "title": "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Integrating Factors"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "aa160337-8256-5561-b72f-4eb286d87c12",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\left(4\\right)y=16,\\quad y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=16.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & =e^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =e^{4 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=e^{4 x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{4 x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & =e^{4 x}\\cdot 16 \\\\ e^{4 x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4 e^{4 x}y & =16 e^{4 x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{4 x}) & =16 e^{4 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ye^{4 x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 16 e^{4 x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ ye^{4 x} & =16\\left(\\frac{1}{4} e^{4 x}\\right)+C \\\\ ye^{4 x} & =4 e^{4 x}+C \\\\ y & =\\left(C + 4 e^{4 x}\\right) e^{- 4 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =\\frac{(4 e^{4 (0)})+C}{(e^{4 (0)})} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{4+C}{1} \\\\ C & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4 - 5 e^{- 4 x}.\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
